Organizing directory nested inside a described archive, exercising the case satx-shape-and-purpose v0.0.8 calls most likely to be got wrong: the boundary sits inside described territory rather than outside it. Holds this language's interface message catalog, a gettext .po file, once one exists: no sidecar, no work, no Dublin Core. Per SAT Sidecars: Config and Metadata v0.0.13, a catalog lives in the archive of the language it translates to, not under lib/locale/; only the language-neutral .pot template lives there. Empty for now, since sat's interface strings are still in the Python source and have not been extracted.
